## 9. STUDENT PORTAL UI/UX

PRIMARY EXPERIENCE:

Help students understand their capabilities, identify learning needs, discover opportunities, and take meaningful development actions.

### A. Student Overview

Top section:
- Personalized greeting.
- Student profile identity.
- Program and semester.
- Current development goals.

Summary section:
- Learning progress.
- Assessed competencies.
- Active learning activities.
- Upcoming deadlines.

Skill section:
- Competency clusters.
- Micro-skill progress.
- Priority skill gaps.
- Evidence status.

Recommendation section:
- Recommended next action.
- Recommended learning resources.
- Relevant opportunities.
- Explanation of recommendations.

The interface must prioritize useful actions.

Do not display large metrics merely to fill dashboard space.

### B. My Skills

Create an understandable competency exploration experience.

Display:
- Competency clusters.
- Individual micro-skills.
- Mastery state.
- Evidence source.
- Assessment date.
- Prerequisite dependencies.

Allow students to:
- Select a competency.
- Explore connected micro-skills.
- View prerequisites.
- View assessment evidence they are authorized to access.
- Identify missing evidence.
- Review development suggestions.

Use an interactive skill map only when it adds clarity.

Provide an accessible alternative list or table.

### C. My Learning

Display two separate sections:

Academic Learning Path:
- Formal course-related learning.
- Lecturer-assigned activities.
- Course learning outcomes.
- Required assessments.

Personal Growth Path:
- Student-selected goals.
- Additional skills.
- Independent resources.
- Portfolio projects.
- Personal development activities.

Do not mix formal academic obligations with optional personal development.

### D. Opportunity Discovery

Create an opportunity exploration interface.

Support:
- Search.
- Category filtering.
- Deadline filtering.
- Eligibility filtering.
- Relevance sorting.
- Saved opportunities.
- Opportunity details.

Opportunity cards display:
- Opportunity title.
- Organization.
- Category.
- Deadline.
- Eligibility status.
- Relevant competency indicators.
- Recommendation explanation.
- Save action.

Opportunity details display:
- Description.
- Requirements.
- Application information.
- Required skills.
- Relevant student skills.
- Skill gaps.
- Recommended preparation.
- Verified source link.

### E. Portfolio

Display:
- Projects.
- Certificates.
- Learning evidence.
- Lecturer-approved evidence.
- Personal achievements.

Make the distinction between self-submitted and institutionally validated evidence visible.

### F. Student Interaction Standards

Use clear action labels:

- Start Learning.
- View Skill Details.
- Submit Evidence.
- Review Recommendation.
- Save Opportunity.
- Check Eligibility.
- Explore Learning Path.

Avoid ambiguous labels such as "Go", "Continue Here", or "Click Me".

