## 14. RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Test the application at:

MOBILE:
360px, 390px, 430px.

TABLET:
768px, 1024px.

DESKTOP:
1280px, 1440px.

LARGE DESKTOP:
1920px.

### Responsive rules

At 360–639px:
- Single-column content.
- Collapsible drawer navigation.
- Stacked cards.
- Full-width primary actions where useful.
- Tables converted to readable cards or controlled horizontal scrolling.
- No horizontal page overflow.

At 640–1023px:
- Two-column layouts where appropriate.
- Compact navigation.
- Simplified dashboard summaries.
- Responsive graph controls.

At 1024–1439px:
- Desktop sidebar.
- Responsive multi-column grids.
- Full dashboard navigation.

At 1440px and above:
- Maximum content width 1440px.
- Maintain readable line lengths.
- Avoid stretching cards unnecessarily.
- Use balanced whitespace.

All pages must support mobile scrolling without hidden important information.

Graph visualizations may use an accessible simplified view on mobile.

