## 15. INTERACTION AND MICRO-INTERACTION RULES

All interactive elements must work.

Examples:

Navigation:
- Active menu state.
- Route transitions.
- Breadcrumb updates.
- Back navigation.

Forms:
- Input validation.
- Required fields.
- Save and cancel.
- Confirmation.
- Success and error feedback.

Cards:
- Interactive cards navigate to actual destinations.
- Static cards must not falsely appear clickable.

Buttons:
- Every button must have a defined action.
- No decorative action buttons.
- No empty click handlers.

Loading:
- Show skeletons or appropriate indicators.

Data updates:
- Refresh visible data after successful changes.
- Provide optimistic updates only when rollback and error handling are implemented.

Modal:
- Correct focus management.
- Escape handling where appropriate.
- Accessible close controls.

Animations:
- 150ms ease-out for fast interactions.
- 200ms ease-out for standard transitions.
- Respect reduced-motion settings.
- Avoid unnecessary motion.

